# MTS Exolve numbers

The handbook is the live page `https://docs.exolve.ru/docs/ru/api-reference/numbering-api/` and its child pages for the reference, free numbers, and purchased numbers. Read it again before any MTS Exolve change. It can change. Do not invent methods, paths, or fields. Do not commit a copy of that page or of the Postman collection.

The host is the literal `https://api.exolve.ru`. HTTPS only. Do not follow redirects. Do not trust a custom certificate. Timeout 30s. Body cap 20 MB. `Content-Type` is `application/json`. POST is the transport. It is not a mutation. `Authorization: Bearer` is sent only to that host.

This release may send only:

- `POST /number/customer/v1/GetList` for purchased numbers. The unfiltered body is exactly `{limit, offset}`. `limit` is 1000. A layer may add `type_name`, then `category_id`, then `region_id`. No `application_uuid`, dates, search, or `sip_filter`.
- `POST /number/reference/v1/GetList` with body `{}`.
- `POST /number/v1/GetFree` for one directory cell, and for at most two Moscow probes before those cells. The cell body is `type_id`, `region_id`, `category_id`, `limit` 500, and `offset`. `random` is `false`, unless the Moscow probe with `random: false` is empty and the same probe without `random` returns a number. Then every cell omits `random`. `random: true` is not sent. No mask. Probe rows are not staged.

Do not call Lock, Unlock, Buy, Delete, GetInfo, SetCallForwarding, DeleteCallForwarding, GetAttributes, SetAmdState, SetCallRecordState, or any other method. The method and the path are literals in the client. Do not accept a path, a field, or a filter from a caller, a flag, or a saved catalog.

Purchased completeness is `accepted === total`. The next offset grows by the rows received. An empty page before that total is a gap and starts the layered re-read. Child totals must sum to the parent. A purchased duplicate fails the walk. After the purchased read, one unfiltered recount compares `total` only. A missing or null `numbers` array with `total` 0, and an object with no fields, is an empty purchased page. A missing, null, or empty `numbers` array with `total` greater than 0 is an empty page and starts the layered re-read. Rows already accepted are not published. A list without `total` fails the page. A root `error` fails the page.

A category whose type is missing adds that type. A type with no categories does not fail the directory. A repeated category on the same type is skipped. A repeated `region_id` keeps the first row. An unreadable `parent_region_id` is empty and the row stays. A missing `regions` array, or an empty one, does not publish. Free cells are DEF `1104`, ABC `1105`, and KDU `1106`, plus any other type that has a category. When one of those three types has no categories, its cells use the handbook category ids: DEF `10000`, `10010`, `10020`, `10030`, `10040`, `10050`; ABC `10001`, `10011`, `10021`, `10031`, `10041`, `10051`; KDU `10002`, `10012`, `10022`, `10032`, `10042`, `10052`. A type that already has categories does not gain that table. KDU uses only region `10084`. When that region is absent, KDU cells are skipped and the other types are still read. Other types use every `region_id`.

A free cell ends only on an empty page. A page shorter or longer than 500 does not end the cell. The next offset grows by the rows received. An empty page after numbers were received is repeated once at the same offset. The first empty page is an empty cell and is not repeated. The next free offset must not pass 5000000. Above that the walk does not publish a short list. An object with no `numbers` and any other field fails that cell. A missing `numbers` array on an otherwise empty object, or null `numbers`, is an empty free page. The same number in a later free cell keeps the first price. The same number in both drafts stays purchased. The access check reads one purchased page, the directory, and the first free cell with `random: false`. It does not probe and does not publish.

A number is the digit string the tariff split already accepts. Do not convert 8 to 7. Free `install_fee` is «Покупка» and `subscription_fee` is «Абонплата». A null, negative, non-decimal, or scientific price leaves that cell empty. Purchased `install_fee` is «Покупка» and `subscription_fee` is «Абонплата». The same empty-price rule applies, and the number stays. `type_name`, `category_name`, `region_name`, and `description` are not stored. City, region, ABC, and the local number come from the tariff fragment. The provider literal is `MTS Exolve`.

Transport, timeout, an empty body, non-JSON, and HTTP 5xx retry once. HTTP 4xx and a body over 20 MB do not. The key stays ciphertext. Do not log the key, the header, the body, the URL, a phone number, or a price. An API key cannot call these routes. The stage logs are `data/numbering-sync/exolve-purchased.txt` and `data/numbering-sync/exolve-free.txt`. A purchased load replaces only purchased rows. A free load replaces only free rows.
